sequenceDiagram
    participant Browser as Browser / Client
    participant Envoy as Envoy Proxy<br/>(ext_authz)
    participant KAP as kube-auth-proxy<br/>4180/TCP (HTTP) or 8443/TCP (HTTPS)
    participant OIDC as OIDC Provider<br/>(Keycloak/Dex)<br/>443/TCP HTTPS
    participant OSOAUTH as OpenShift OAuth<br/>443/TCP HTTPS
    participant OSUSER as OpenShift User API<br/>443/TCP HTTPS
    participant K8SAPI as Kubernetes API Server<br/>443/TCP HTTPS
    participant Redis as Redis<br/>6379/TCP (optional TLS)
    participant Upstream as Upstream Application<br/>Configurable

    rect rgb(230, 245, 255)
        Note over Browser,Upstream: Flow 1: OIDC Authentication
        Browser->>KAP: GET /oauth2/start<br/>HTTP/HTTPS, TLS 1.2+
        KAP->>OIDC: 302 Redirect to /authorize<br/>HTTPS, TLS 1.2+, Client ID
        Browser->>OIDC: User authenticates<br/>HTTPS, TLS 1.2+
        OIDC->>KAP: GET /oauth2/callback<br/>HTTPS, TLS 1.2+, Auth code
        KAP->>OIDC: POST /token<br/>HTTPS, TLS 1.2+, Client creds + code
        OIDC-->>KAP: Access token + ID token
        KAP->>OIDC: GET /userinfo (optional)<br/>HTTPS, TLS 1.2+, Bearer token
        OIDC-->>KAP: User claims
        KAP->>Redis: Store session (if Redis backend)<br/>TCP/TLS, Password/ACL
        KAP-->>Browser: Set-Cookie: _oauth2_proxy<br/>HTTP/HTTPS
        Browser->>KAP: Request with session cookie<br/>HTTP/HTTPS, TLS 1.2+
        KAP->>Upstream: Proxied request<br/>+ X-Forwarded-User, Email, Groups, Access-Token
        Upstream-->>KAP: Response
        KAP-->>Browser: Proxied response
    end

    rect rgb(255, 243, 224)
        Note over Envoy,KAP: Flow 2: Envoy ext_authz Check
        Envoy->>KAP: GET /oauth2/auth<br/>HTTP/HTTPS, TLS 1.2+<br/>Forwarded cookie/Bearer
        KAP->>KAP: Validate session<br/>(cookie or token)
        alt Authenticated
            KAP-->>Envoy: 202 Accepted<br/>+ X-Forwarded-User headers
        else Not Authenticated
            KAP-->>Envoy: 401 Unauthorized
        end
    end

    rect rgb(232, 245, 233)
        Note over Browser,Upstream: Flow 3: K8s Service Account Token
        Browser->>KAP: Request with Bearer SA token<br/>HTTP/HTTPS, TLS 1.2+
        KAP->>K8SAPI: POST TokenReview<br/>HTTPS, TLS 1.2+, SA token
        K8SAPI-->>KAP: TokenReview response<br/>(authenticated: true/false)
        KAP->>Upstream: Proxied request<br/>+ X-Forwarded-User=system:serviceaccount:ns:sa
        Upstream-->>KAP: Response
        KAP-->>Browser: Proxied response
    end

    rect rgb(248, 232, 235)
        Note over Browser,Upstream: Flow 4: OpenShift OAuth
        Browser->>KAP: GET /oauth2/start<br/>HTTP/HTTPS, TLS 1.2+
        KAP->>OSOAUTH: GET /.well-known/oauth-authorization-server<br/>HTTPS, TLS 1.2+
        OSOAUTH-->>KAP: OAuth metadata
        KAP->>OSOAUTH: 302 Redirect to /authorize<br/>HTTPS, TLS 1.2+, Client ID
        Browser->>OSOAUTH: User authenticates<br/>HTTPS, TLS 1.2+
        OSOAUTH->>KAP: GET /oauth2/callback<br/>HTTPS, TLS 1.2+, Auth code
        KAP->>OSOAUTH: POST /token<br/>HTTPS, TLS 1.2+, Client creds + code
        OSOAUTH-->>KAP: Access token
        KAP->>OSUSER: GET /apis/user.openshift.io/v1/users/~<br/>HTTPS, TLS 1.2+, Bearer token
        OSUSER-->>KAP: User identity
        KAP->>Upstream: Proxied request<br/>+ Identity headers
    end
